{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794081107,"nonce":"xjtTuCZz5dpvIIFUsbP4e0xSPB8=","title":"Design documents by aspect, each saying what holds now and why","message":"One design document per feature went out of date as later features revised earlier ones: what held for one part of the system was spread over six or seven documents, each a snapshot of its day, and had to be replayed in order.\n\nDecisions (2026-11-07, Luis):\n\n- doc/design is one document per aspect: store, issue, schema, query, cli, flows, tui, views, jira, migration. Each says what holds now and why; no history, no plan, no deferred list.\n- A story's design is written on the story issue and approved there. The change that builds it updates the aspect documents, so they never describe what is not built.\n- Code cites a decision by document and heading, `(doc/design/views.md, \"The ghost\")`, not by a numbered id: the old ids collided across documents. TestDesignCitations makes a renamed heading fail instead of rot.\n- History-only documents (fork-foundations, the pre-fork architecture, bridges/jira.md) are deleted; git keeps them. Designs found unbuilt move to their story issues.\n\nThe rules are in AGENTS.md, Working conventions.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["infra"],"status":"in-progress","type":"story"}}]}